# Paths excluded from Semgrep SAST. Shipped application code stays scanned.
#
# Rule: exclude a path only when you have TRIAGED its findings and they are
# false positives, non-shipped tooling, or documentation examples. Write down
# which finding each entry silences — an unexplained exclusion is how a real
# vulnerability hides.
#
# Prefer a GLOB over a fixed path. A path-pinned entry fails open the moment
# the file moves, and it does so silently: the exclusion simply stops matching
# and the gate goes red for a reason nobody connects to the move.

# Local agent tooling — hooks, agents, commands. Not shipped.
# (Typical source of path-join traversal findings in the migration hook.)
.claude/

# Generated knowledge-graph output — not source.
graphify-out/

# Build / CI / migration scripts — not shipped to the runtime.
# (Typical source of non-literal-regexp findings in the budget checker.)
scripts/

# Documentation — example tokens and hashes are illustrative, not secrets.
*.md
docs/*.py
docs/**/*.py

# Test fixtures — example hashes used as test data.
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
